add('cs-1c-mclaws-semmes', 'engagement', '(July 2, evening)', 'to the right of the line near the ravine; Semmes mortally wounded as the brigade moved toward the right', "Kershaw: General Semmes promptly responded to his call and put his brigade in motion toward the right, preparatory to moving to the front; while his troops were moving he fell mortally wounded; one regiment of Semmes's brigade came at a double-quick as far as the ravine in the rear and checked the Federals.",
    'BL3', 'BL3-S033', "Greneral Semmes promptl}^ responded to my call, and put his brigade in motion toward the right", 'inferred', author=KE, date='1863-07-02', reasoning="A sister brigade commander's account.", extra_quote="he fell, mortally wounded", ocr_uncertain=True, note='OCR "Greneral"/"promptl}^".')
add('cs-1c-mclaws', 'march', 'About 11 o’clock on the morning of the 2d; McLaws’s division in advance, with Hood following', 'the march under the conduct of engineer officers, concealed from Federal view toward the position for the attack on the Federal left', "Longstreet: about 11 o'clock on the morning of July 2 Lee ordered the march, put under the conduct of engineer officers to move by the best route and conceal the movement from the Federals; McLaws's division was in advance with Hood following; the advance began at half-past 3 in the afternoon.",
    'BL3', 'BL3-S034', "About 11 o'clock on the morning of the 2d he ordered the march", 'inferred', author=LS, t_iso='1863-07-02T11:00', date='1863-07-02', reasoning="Longstreet was the corps commander (not an officer of McLaws's division) writing after the war.", road='toward the Emmitsburg road (following up the direction of the Emmitsburg road)',
    extra_quote="the advance was ordered — at half-past 3 o'clock in the afternoon", gaz='GZ-041', note="OR D ledger carries the McLaws and Longstreet reports; Law (Hood's division) places the division on the Chambersburg road a mile from the town and then moved right 'traversing the angle between the Chambersburg and Emmitsburg roads'.")
# ---- Stuart's cavalry (Hunt, Union; Mosby, Confederate scout of Stuart's command but not present)
for u, who in (('cs-cav-flee', 'Fitzhugh Lee'), ('cs-cav-chambliss', 'Chambliss')):
    add(u, 'march', 'on the night of the 24th (June); ford of the Potomac near Seneca on the night of the 27th', "round the Army of the Potomac between it and Centreville into Maryland: the Potomac forded near Seneca (20 miles above Washington), Rockville, Westminster, Union Mills (encamped on the 29th)", "Hunt: Stuart with the brigades of Hampton, Fitzhugh Lee and Chambliss started on the night of June 24 to ride round the Army of the Potomac, was forced east and forded the Potomac near Seneca on the night of June 27, marched north by Rockville (capturing a wagon train), pushed on through Westminster (sharp action with a Delaware squadron) to Union Mills and encamped there on the 29th.",
        'BL3', 'BL3-S028', "forced him so far east that he was compelled to ford the Potomac near Seneca", 'inferred', author=HU, date='1863-06-27', reasoning='A Union general\'s post-war summary of the Confederate march.',
        extra_quote="through Westminster, where he had a sharp action with a squadron of Delaware horse", road='Rockville - Westminster - Union Mills (outside the loaded ground)')
    add(u, 'march', 'on the morning of the 30th (June); about 10 A. M. Chambliss reached Hanover', 'across country from Union Mills to Hanover, Chambliss in front and Hampton in rear of the 200-wagon train, Fitzhugh Lee well out on the left flank', "Hunt: learning the Federal cavalry in strong force at Littlestown barred his direct road to Gettysburg, Stuart moved across country on the morning of June 30 to Hanover, Chambliss in front and Hampton in rear of his long train of two hundred wagons, Fitzhugh Lee well out on the left flank; about 10 A. M. Chambliss reaching Hanover found Kilpatrick passing through and attacked him but was driven out before Hampton or Lee could support.",
        'BL3', 'BL3-S028', "he moved across country to Hanover, Chambliss in front and Hampton in rear", 'inferred', author=HU, t_iso='1863-06-30T10:00', date='1863-06-30', approx=True, reasoning='A Union general\'s post-war summary of the Confederate march.', conflicts=['POS-E-US-CAV-3D-FARNSWORTH-18PA-002'],
        extra_quote="About 10 A. M. Chambliss, reaching Han- over, found Kilpatrick", note="Union side at Hanover: the 18th PA (Phillips) and the 5th NY (about 10 o'clock); the Michigan address (Kidd) puts the 6th Michigan's skirmishing soon after noon. All carried.")
    add(u, 'march', 'a night march for York (June 30 to July 1); that night (July 1) he learned Lee was concentrating at Gettysburg; left for that place next day (July 2)', 'to York, to Carlisle, then to Gettysburg', "Hunt: Stuart made a night march for York only to learn that Early had left the day before; pushing on to Carlisle he found Ewell gone and the place held by militia under General W. F. Smith (demand refused, shells thrown into the town, government barracks burned); that night he learned Lee's army was concentrating at Gettysburg and left for that place next day.",
        'BL3', 'BL3-S028', "he made a night march for York, only to learn that Early had left the day before", 'inferred', author=HU, date='1863-07-02', reasoning='A Union general\'s post-war summary.', ocr_uncertain=False,
        extra_quote="That night he learned that Lee's army was concentrating at Gettysbui'g", conflicts=['POS-E-US-CAV-3D-FARNSWORTH-18PA-003'],
        note="Hunt gives no road for the final approach; Kidd (Michigan address) has the head of Hampton's column at Hunterstown late in the afternoon of July 2 and Stuart reaching the army the evening of July 2; on July 3 the York turnpike and the Stallsmith farm road (POS-E-CS-CAV-DIV-002).")
add('cs-cav-jenkins', 'march', 'On the 8th (June)', "as Ewell's advance into the valley (Jenkins's brigade sent ahead of the other five brigades of Stuart)", "Hunt: on June 8 General Lee, having sent Jenkins's brigade as Ewell's advance into the valley, reviewed the other five brigades of Stuart (10,292 combatants) near Brandy Station.",
    'BL3', 'BL3-S028', "having sent Jenkins's brigade as Ewell's advance into the valley", 'inferred', author=HU, date='1863-06-08', reasoning='A Union general\'s post-war summary.', note="Earlier march only (no Gettysburg-day position in BL3). Jenkins's day positions on July 3 come from Kidd (POS-E-CS-CAV-JENKINS-001).")
